# Web Use Backends — Public Configuration Template

This template contains no real credentials.

## Canonical order

1. Search or fetch for public information.
2. Managed browser for ordinary rendered automation.
3. Browserless for protected extraction.
4. TinyFish for deeper hosted stealth-browser control.
5. Domain-owned structured API when justified.
6. Verified visible handoff for login or manual approval.

The managed browser may be headless. Do not call it person-facing unless the
deployment proves a visible co-interaction lane.

## Credential pattern

Load secrets at runtime through your approved secret manager or environment.
Never hardcode them in a skill, committed file, log, or chat.

```bash
BROWSERLESS_TOKEN="<runtime value>" \
  python3 skills/web-use/scripts/browserless_extract.py \
  "<URL>" \
  --mode stealth-bql

TINYFISH_API_KEY="<runtime value>" \
  python3 skills/web-use/scripts/tinyfish_browser_extract.py \
  "<URL>"
```

## Browserless sessions

Use sessions only for repeated same-site work with a demonstrated persistence
need. Store returned bearer URLs in a `0600` local file, redact normal output,
stop the remote session when finished, and delete the local session file.

## Visible browser rule

A browser being installed, running, Chromium-based, or extension-compatible does
not prove external attachment. Verify the named app, page readiness, login,
consent boundary, and takeover path before using it.
